---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
---

<Layout title="About — Danny Silva | Personal Blog" activeNav="about">
    <main>
        <section class="about-hero">
            <div class="about-image">
                <Image src="/assets/danny.png" alt="Author portrait" width={400} height={400} />
            </div>
            <div class="about-intro">
                <h1>A blog for the things I am still <span>thinking through</span></h1>
                <div class="about-text">
                    <p>Hey, I'm Danny. This is not a portfolio. It is a personal blog about the private weather of my mind: philosophy, art, attention, books, tools, systems, doubts, and whatever else refuses to leave quietly.</p>
                    <p>I try to write stoically, which to me means plainly, without performance, and with some respect for what I do not know yet. Some posts are essays. Some are notes. Some are records of what I am reading, building, watching, or trying to understand.</p>
                    <p>The point is not to present a finished self. The point is to keep evidence of the search.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="philosophy">
            <h3 class="philosophy-title">What Keeps Returning</h3>
            <div class="philosophy-grid">
                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
                            <path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Attention Is a Moral Resource</h3>
                    <p>What I attend to becomes part of what I become. I am interested in fewer distractions, cleaner thought, and a life that can be examined without rushing.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5z"/>
                            <path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5"/>
                            <path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Beauty Changes Conduct</h3>
                    <p>Art, rooms, interfaces, rituals, and sentences all train the eye. I write about the forms that make ordinary life feel more deliberate.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                            <path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"/>
                            <path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"/>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Work Belongs Beside Wonder</h3>
                    <p>What I build and what I think about are not separate lives. Technical notes sit next to philosophy because both are attempts to make sense of the world.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
